     uunnvviiss — revert a visual representation of data back to original form

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     uunnvviiss [--ee] [--HHhh | --mm] [_f_i_l_e _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     uunnvviiss is the inverse function of vis(1).  It reverts a visual representa‐
     tion of data back to its original form on standard output.

     The options are as follows:

     --ee      Don't decode \ escaped sequences.

     --HH      Decode entity references and numeric character references from
             RFC 1866.  (VIS_HTTP1866)

     --hh      Decode using the URI encoding from RFC 1808.  (VIS_HTTP1808)

     --mm      Decode using mime style.  (VIS_MIMESTYLE)

     Mixing --hh or --HH with --mm is not supported.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     vis(1), unvis(3), vis(3)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The uunnvviiss command appears in 4.4BSD.

